According to a report by IntelMarketResearch, the global Steel Strand for Bridge Cables Market was valued at USD 4,815 million in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 6,986 million by 2034, expanding at a CAGR of 5.5% during 2025–2034. Steel strand for bridge cables is a high-strength structural material manufactured by stranding multiple high-tensile steel wires, commonly in seven- or nineteen-wire configurations. Corrosion protection through hot-dip galvanizing, zinc-aluminum alloy coating and epoxy coating enables reliable performance in suspension, cable-stayed and arch bridges.
