Regional Outlook
Europe was the largest market in 2025, supported by mature infrastructure programs, bridge renewal initiatives and stringent safety and sustainability requirements.
Asia-Pacific is the fastest-growing region, driven by rapid urbanization, highway and high-speed rail development and expanding bridge construction.
North America is seeing increased demand from rehabilitation of legacy bridge structures and the need for improved durability.
South America is developing opportunities through bridge revitalization and public-private infrastructure projects.
The Middle East & Africa region is investing in bridge infrastructure to support expanding population centers and strategic trade corridors.
Why This Market Matters
Steel strands are critical load-bearing components in modern cable-supported bridges. Their combination of tensile strength, fatigue resistance and corrosion protection makes them suitable for demanding structural applications.
Manufacturers are increasingly investing in advanced coatings, high-strength alloys, localized production and strategic partnerships. At the same time, raw-material volatility and shortages of high-grade steel billets remain challenges for suppliers and infrastructure contractors.
The report indicates that global production capacity is close to 3.5 million tons per year, while industry gross profit margins are generally in the 18%–25% range, reflecting the value added by coating technology and stringent quality controls.
